# Reflection - Unit 2: Building App UI

## What I Learned
- How to apply conditionals, classes, function types, and lambda expressions in Kotlin.
- How applications can respond to user interactions, such as button clicks.
- How state can be managed to calculate and update values, such as in a tip calculator.

## Challenges
- Learning how lambda expressions and function types work required additional practice.
- Practicing UI interactions using only Kotlin was more limited than using Android Studio.
- Connecting programming logic with user interface behavior was a new learning experience.

## My Choices
- I created Kotlin-based simulations for button clicks and state management to strengthen my logic outside Android Studio.
- I used simple examples, including score evaluation and a tip calculator, to improve my understanding of the fundamentals.
- I kept my code clear and organized by using readable structures and helpful comments.

## Outcome
Unit 2 improved my understanding of Kotlin fundamentals and introduced me to the concepts behind interactive applications.  
Although the activities did not fully use the Android Studio interface, I practiced the logic behind button interactions and state management, preparing me for more complete app development in later units.
